.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt HARNESSATOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm harnessator
.Nd package manager and policy layer for AI coding harness configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar flags
.Op Ar args
.Pp
where
.Ar command
is one of:
.Ic version , validate , init , setup , update , verify , doctor ,
list , search , scan , harvest , info , why , enable , disable ,
.Cm "source add" ,
.Cm "source remove" ,
.Cm "source list" ,
.Cm "source new" ,
.Cm "provider use" ,
.Cm "provider show" ,
.Cm "provider none" ,
.Cm "dev" ,
.Cm "dev status" ,
.Cm "dev sync" ,
.Cm "dev drop" ,
.Ic contribute , serve , tui
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
configures AI coding harnesses
.Pq opencode , Claude Code , Codex , Antigravity , pi , Cursor
from governed git sources: rules, skills, prompts, workflows, sub-agents,
hooks, tools, MCP servers and provider/model policies.
The registry is git - access control, review and provenance come from your
forge; there is no server component.
.Pp
Project configuration
.Pq Xr harnessator.toml 5
declares sources and selections;
.Nm Cm setup
resolves refs to exact commits, exports read-only checkouts into the
per-user store
.Pa ~/.harnessator ,
computes a deterministic plan with provenance, renders each target
harness's native layout, and writes the committed lockfile
.Pq Xr harnessator.lock 5 .
.Nm Cm verify
is the CI gate that fails when anything diverges from the lock.
.Ss Concepts
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Components
typed units addressed as
.Dq Ar source:category/name :
rule, skill, prompt, workflow, agent, hook, tool, mcp, provider, policy.
.It Sources
git repositories with a
.Em harnessator.toml
manifest of kind
.Dq source .
A source may import child sources, so a corporate root can form the entry
point of a source graph.
.It Layers
corporate, team, project, personal - each adds sources and
refines selections; every enablement carries provenance
queryable with
.Nm Cm why .
.It Pins
refs in the config are tag ranges or branches; the lock records resolved
commit SHAs and sha256 content digests per component, making config drift
reviewable in ordinary git history.
.It Adapters
per-harness renderers. A component type without a native slot on a target
is reported as a loud skip, never silently dropped.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm version
Print
.Nm
and its build-stamped version.
.It Cm validate Op Fl -check-paths Ar file ...
Schema-check source manifests and project configs; reports all problems at
once; rejects unknown keys.
With no arguments, validates
.Pa ./harnessator.toml .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -check-paths
verify that component paths exist relative to each manifest.
.El
.It Cm init Op Fl -targets Ar list Op Fl -source Ar url ... Fl -ref Ar expr Op Fl -manifest Ar path Fl -force Op Ar dir
Create a managed project: canonical
.Pa harnessator.toml ,
a
.Pa .gitignore
block for generated artifacts, and
.Pa AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md
redirect entry files if absent.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -targets Ar list
comma-separated harness targets
(default
.Dq opencode,claude ) .
.It Fl -source Ar urls
comma-separated git source URLs; names default to repo basenames.
.It Fl -ref Ar expr
ref expression for
.Fl -source
(default
.Dq main ) .
.It Fl -force
overwrite an existing config.
.El
.It Cm setup Op Fl -dry-run Op Fl -config Ar path
Fetch, resolve, export, plan, materialize, write the lock.
Refuses to write the lock while any source is in dev mode.
Ends with a restart-your-harness notice.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -dry-run
print plan and would-write report; touch nothing.
.El
.It Cm update
alias of
.Cm setup
(re-resolving refs is the update).
.It Cm verify Op Fl -config Ar path
Compare on-disk state to
.Pa harnessator.lock :
checkout markers, per-component content digests;
dev-mode sources skipped.
Exit 1 on drift - the CI gate.
.It Cm check Op Fl -json Op Fl -quiet Op Fl -install-hook Ar hook Op Fl -remove-hook Ar hook Op Fl -config Ar path
Offline enforcement gate: strict model policy, lock
digest integrity and installed-state drift in one command with a clean
exit code - lock pins only, never fetches.
.Fl -json
emits
.Dq ok / problems / warnings
as one machine-readable object;
.Fl -quiet
is silent unless failing.
.Fl -install-hook Ar hook
(pre-commit or pre-push) installs a managed marker block in
.Pa .git/hooks/
that runs
.Cm check Fl -quiet
and self-skips in unmanaged repos;
.Fl -remove-hook
deletes only harnessator-installed hooks, refusing foreign files.
.It Cm doctor Op Fl -config Ar path
verify plus lock freshness, adapter-spec diffs
(missing, wrong, stray or blocked links) and gitignore hygiene.
.It Cm list Op Fl -all Op Fl -config Ar path
Enabled components with provenance;
.Fl -all
also lists skips with reasons.
.It Cm search Ar text Op Fl -config Ar path
Substring search over fetched manifests; each hit prefixed
.Ic on
or
.Ic off ;
exit 1 when nothing matched.
.It Cm index build
Re-index the current project's pinned sources into the store-level
registry index
.Pa ~/.harnessator/cache/index.json ;
entries of other sources are kept.
.It Cm index search Op Fl -category Ar cat Op Ar text
Query the registry index without project context - no lock, no network.
Exit 1 when nothing matched.
.It Cm index show Ar ref
Full provenance (source, git, pin, path, tags, license) of one indexed
component.
.It Cm mcp serve Op Fl -config Ar path
Read-only MCP server (JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio) exposing the current
project's configuration to agents:
.Ic search , Ic list_active , Ic why ,
.Ic component_content , Ic policy_status .
Component reads come from the pinned store checkout the lock digests
cover; mutations stay CLI-only.
.It Cm scan Op Fl -json Ar path ...
Read-only cold-start report over project trees or loose directories
(default
.Pa . ) :
components found via the adapters' Recognize layer (the read-side
counterpart of the writers - symmetry-tested), listed with category, id
and content digest; symlinked entries classified
.Ic managed Ns / Ic external
and never harvested; sanitize hits (secret shapes, personal paths) as
masked
.Em file:line
findings.
Across roots, same-id components cluster as
.Ic identical
(dedupe candidates) or
.Dv DIVERGENT
(the stale-copy problem, visible). Config-embedded components are
detected too: MCP servers in any harness style (canonicalized before
digesting) and claude hook scripts referenced from settings files.
.Fl json
emits the stable versioned envelope
.Pq schema , generated , roots[] , clusters[]
designed to also feed a future
.Em status
command and the web-GUI sprawl view without migration.
Exit 0 whenever the scan completed; findings are not failures.
.It Cm harvest Op Fl -name Ar id Op Fl -into Ar dir Op Fl -prefer Ar how Op Fl -dry-run Op Fl -allow-hits Op Fl -commit Ar dir Op Fl -adopt Ar path ...
Publishes scanned candidates as a validated source repo. Guarantees: inputs never modified; all-or-nothing -
divergent copies, sanitize findings and invalid ids abort before any
write. Identical copies merge;
.Fl -prefer Ar newest|largest
resolves divergent ones. A
.Fl -into Ar dir
re-run is idempotent (digest-matching components skip, the manifest stays
byte-stable). Lifted cursor rules keep their frontmatter as manifest
hints (exact round-trip with the adapter); MCP servers embedded in any
harness config style (.mcp.json, .cursor/mcp.json,
.agents/mcp_config.json, opencode.json, codex config.toml) are
normalized, merged into the source's shared mcp/servers.json with all
per-target shapes regenerated, and deduped across styles by digest;
claude hook commands referencing in-project scripts lift the script to
.Ic hooks/shared/
with a rewritten template. New sources get
.Em git init
and a first commit; manifest components receive an
.Ic origin
provenance field, and fresh sources get a
.Ic default
profile selecting everything.
Entries matching no rule are listed in
.Pa harvest-report.json
(with external symlinks as context); the guided tail
.Pq the harnessator-harvest skill
works through them and ratifies with
.Fl commit Ar dir ,
which re-validates the source and commits it - agent drafts, tool judges.
.Fl adopt
additionally turns each donor project into a consumer of the published
source: its originals are replaced by managed links only after a digest
proves byte-identical content (divergent ones are kept and reported;
existing generated paths are backed up as
.Pa *.pre-adopt ) .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -name Ar id
new source id, created as
.Pa ./ Ns Ar id
(a path is accepted; its base becomes the id).
.It Fl -into Ar dir
extend an existing source directory.
.It Fl -prefer Ar how
resolve divergent copies:
.Ar newest
or
.Ar largest .
.It Fl -dry-run
print the write plan; write nothing.
.It Fl -allow-hits
publish despite sanitize findings (review them first).
.El
.It Cm info Ar ref Op Fl -config Ar path
Full details of one component: pin, absolute store path, provenance,
targets, tags, capabilities, description.
.It Cm layers Op Fl -config Ar path
Show the scope-layer files the project resolves from: each path, present
or absent, and what it contributes (sources, templates, includes,
provider, policy, corporate markers). The merge, made visible.
.It Cm why Ar ref Op Fl -config Ar path
Why a component is enabled or skipped, incl. which template selects it.
.It Cm enable Ar ref Op Fl -layer Ar name Op Fl -config Ar path
Add a template
.Pq Ar source:profile
or a
.Ic select
include
.Pq Ar cat/id No or Ar source:cat/id
and rewrite the config canonically.
Run
.Cm setup
afterwards.
.It Cm disable Ar ref Op Fl -layer Ar name Op Fl -config Ar path
Remove a template or add an exclude.
Refuses components marked
.Em always .
.It Cm "source add" Ar url Op Fl -ref Ar expr Op Fl -name Ar id Op Fl -layer Ar name Op Fl -manifest Ar path
Declare a git source
.Pq corporate|team|project|personal .
.Fl manifest Ar path
selects a sub-directory manifest for multi-source repos: source identity
becomes the triple
.Pa (git , ref , manifest) ,
so one repository can host several independent sources
.Pq e.g. harnessator's own skills live in a source/ sub-directory .
Duplicate names are rejected.
.It Cm "source remove" Ar name
Undeclare a source; run
.Cm setup
to reconcile.
.It Cm "source list"
Declared sources with resolved pins.
.It Cm "source new" Fl -name Ar id Op Fl -dir Ar path Op Fl -remote Ar kind Op Fl -description Ar text
Scaffold a new component source: self-validating manifest, category
directories, git init and first commit.
.Fl -remote
is one of
.Ic gitlab , azure , github
and creates the repository via
.Ic glab , az , gh
when installed.
.It Cm "provider use" Ar source:provider-id | Cm "provider show" | Cm "provider none"
Select, inspect or clear the provider profile
(see Sx GOVERNANCE ) .
.It Cm dev Ar target Op Fl -branch Ar name
Start an isolated dev overlay of
.Ar target
.Pq a source, or Ar source:cat/id
for this project: a clone of the store checkout on its own branch, wired
into
.Em this
project's links by the next
.Cm setup ;
all other projects keep the read-only pin.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -branch Ar name
overlay branch
(default
.Dq harnessator/dev/<user> ) .
.El
.It Cm "dev status"
List overlays with branch and dirty state.
.It Cm "dev sync" Op Ar source
Fetch and rebase each overlay onto its upstream branch
(branch refs only).
.It Cm "dev drop" Ar source Op Fl -force
Remove an overlay binding and clone; refuses dirty or unpushed work
unless
.Fl -force .
.It Cm contribute Op Ar source Op Fl -title Ar t Op Fl -body Ar b Op Fl -target-branch Ar b
For active overlays: verify commits exist (native git),
.Dq git push -u origin Ar branch ,
then open the merge request via
.Ic glab / az / gh
if installed, else print the exact forge URL.
After merge,
.Cm update
pulls it into your pinned checkout.
.It Cm serve Op Fl -port Ar p Op Fl -config Ar path
Localhost web GUI bound to 127.0.0.1 only (loopback is the trust
boundary): plan, pins, governance, dev state, warnings, and buttons for
.Cm setup / update / verify / doctor
with their full reports.
API:
.Pa /api/state ,
.Pa /api/action .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -port Ar p
port to bind
(default 7070 ) .
.El
.It Cm tui Op Fl -config Ar path
Interactive terminal menu:
.Ic s etup , u pdate , v erify , d octor , l ist ,
.Ic e nable
.Ar ref ,
.Ic x
disable
.Ar ref ,
.Ic w
hy
.Ar ref ,
.Ic q
uit .
.El
.Sh GOVERNANCE
Provider components define an approved model catalog with aliases; policy
components restrict it (
.Em strict
by default) and may pin sub-agent models.
Selection lives in
.Pa harnessator.toml
and is checked inside every command: strict violations block setup, list,
doctor alike; soft ones warn.
Rendering: opencode gets a provider block and a policy-filtered model
list; Claude Code gets an env block including
.Ev CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL ;
codex gets
.Ic model_providers
in the managed block; pi, cursor and antigravity report loud skips.
Secret
.Em values
never appear in configs or generated files - only environment variable
names.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xr harnessator.toml 5
project config and source manifests (both, discriminated by
.Ic kind ) .
.It Xr harnessator.lock 5
generated lockfile: pins and content digests.
.It Pa .harnessator/
per-project generated dir:
.Pa active.md
(the agent-facing index),
.Pa active.json ,
.Pa dev.json ,
tool and pi-package link farms. Gitignored.
.It Pa ~/.harnessator/
per-user store: clones, pinned checkouts, dev overlays,
.Pa personal.toml
fallback layer, cache. Relocate with
.Ev HARNESSATOR_HOME .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev HARNESSATOR_HOME
store directory override (default
.Pa ~/.harnessator ) .
.It Ev LITELLM_API_KEY No and friends
provider
.Ic auth_env
names (harness-rendered, e.g. codex
.Ic env_key )
- consumed by the harnesses, never by
.Nm .
.El
Git authentication uses stock mechanisms (credential helper, SSH agent,
contextual PATs); private https sources generally need
.Dq git config --global credential.helper store
or an SSH URL.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
success.
.It 1
failure - validation, policy violation, drift, git error.
.It 2
usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Govern a new project:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
harnessator init --source https://git.example.com/ai/corp-tools.git \
    --ref '~v1' --targets opencode,claude .
harnessator enable corp-tools:default
harnessator setup
harnessator doctor
.Ed
Improve a skill and upstream it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
harnessator dev corp:skill/jira-issue
harnessator setup
$EDITOR ~/.harnessator/dev/corp/skills/jira-issue/SKILL.md
git -C ~/.harnessator/dev/corp commit -am 'jira-issue: assert AC coverage'
harnessator dev sync && harnessator contribute
# ...merge...
harnessator update
harnessator dev drop corp
.Ed
CI gate:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
harnessator verify   # exit != 0 when anything diverges from harnessator.lock
.Ed
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
MVP targets: opencode, claude, codex, antigravity, pi, cursor.
Expansion targets (gemini, cline, copilot, windsurf) are planned; unknown
targets fail validation.
OS coverage: linux, macOS (symlinks) and Windows (junctions for
directories, copies verified by digests for files).
.Sh CAVEATS
The
.Cm tui
is a first cut (plain menu, no full-screen redraw).
Provider rendering for pi/cursor/antigravity is an explicit loud skip
until their shapes are verified.
Windows junction code is compile-verified only until a Windows runner
exists.
